{
  "method": "23 MACS recordings lasting 10 s at distinct recording sites. Allocate up to three sites per environment (airport, park, public square) and vote stratum (no voice tags, some up to half, or more than half) with at least four annotations. Exclude all sites from prior audio-cues/macs*, level-time, level-time/word-study and ambient-activity panels. Within eligible sites rank files by SHA256(reel-native-voice-2026v1/ + filename); maximum-cardinality minimum-rank assignment to strata. Four slots lacked a site. MACS voice tags are adults_talking, children_voices and announcement_speech. The reader could choose any of the ten original nonblank tags. The human references are each listener\u2019s own tags.",
  "reader": "gpt-6.1-terra via local signed-in Codex. Fresh ephemeral session per recording per revision, only reel.view enabled, anonymous recording.wav, --image-client --tracks sound. Each session received two contiguous MCP views [0,8] and [8,10] through end_of_view, with spectra and local speech, AudioSet and CoNeTTE estimates. Raw WAV input and the optional 30B reader were off. Tag order and instructions were fixed. Neither a filename with a class nor any annotation was supplied. Score is the intersection divided by union of selected tags, 1 for two empty sets. Within each recording compare GPT with every listener and every pair of distinct listeners, then average equally over recordings. The mismatched control pairs each GPT response with every other recording. No joint negatives receive credit for a pair with a nonempty union.",
